1. **A semiconductor device, comprising:**

a semiconductor substrate including first, second, third, and fourth memory-cell regions arranged such that adjacent ones of the memory-cell regions abut one another;

a first active structure extending through the first and second memory-cell regions and defining a first pair of memory cells having a first shared source portion;

a second active structure extending through the third and fourth memory-cell regions and defining a second pair of memory cells having a second shared source portion; and

a conductive structure disposed beneath the first and second active structures and extending across both the first shared source portion and the second shared source portion in a plan view.
